### How does parallelSort work?

```java
BigDecimal[] amounts = loadTransactionAmounts(); // millions of elements
Arrays.parallelSort(amounts);  // parallel merge sort on common ForkJoinPool
```

Internally it goes parallel above ~8192 elements; below that, calls sequential `Arrays.sort`.

### How does parallelPrefix work?

```java
BigDecimal[] dailyNet = loadDailyNetAmounts();
Arrays.parallelPrefix(dailyNet, BigDecimal::add);
// dailyNet[i] is now the cumulative balance through day i
System.out.println("Day 30 cumulative: " + dailyNet[29]);
```

### How does parallelSetAll work?

```java
BigDecimal[] fees = new BigDecimal[1000];
BigDecimal baseFee = new BigDecimal("10.00");
BigDecimal step = new BigDecimal("0.50");
Arrays.parallelSetAll(fees, i -> baseFee.add(step.multiply(BigDecimal.valueOf(i))));
```

### What is the common ForkJoinPool concern?

All three share the common pool with parallel streams. A long parallel operation can delay other parallel work in the same process.

### When does parallel actually pay off?

| Condition | Parallel Helps? |
|-----------|----------------|
| Large array (10K+) | Yes |
| Multi-core machine | Yes |
| Non-trivial per-element cost | Yes |
| Small array (<1K) | No, overhead dominates |
| Single-core | No |
| Cheap comparison | Maybe not |

### What are common interview follow-up questions?

